    "reply": "I added `tests/test_payments.py` with 12 unittest tests covering `shop/payments.py`. `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests` passes: 11 pass and 1 is an expected failure.\n\nThe tests cover:\n- **`line_total`:** multiplication, fractional prices, and zero quantity.\n- **`order_total`:** an empty order, tax on a single line, summing several lines before tax, rounding to cents, and that the input list isn't mutated.\n- **`refund`:** a normal partial refund, a zero refund, and a full refund.\n\n**Possible bug:** `refund` doesn't check the amount, so refunding more than the order total returns a negative balance. I kept that as a `@unittest.expectedFailure` test and left `shop/` untouched. This is my reading of the intended behaviour, so if negative refunds are meant to be allowed, that test should be removed.\n\nNothing under `shop/` was changed, and I haven't committed anything.",
